WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
From contract interface to agent action.
A verified interface becomes an MCP tool. The owner sets policy. Orloj validates, simulates and confirms.
Edited walkthrough from actual captured screens. The working app runs locally.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Register the interface.
Start with a Soroban address, XLM or an issued asset. Registration inspects the interface; it never deploys a contract or grants writes.
Read-only capture of the existing registration screen.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Permission is explicit.
Enable balance reads and selected writes. Unsupported or asset-specific operations remain visibly excluded. Unattended spending grants are currently disabled.
An enabled method is not an unattended signing grant.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Read, without submitting.
The same Testnet balance was read through Soroban and the classic DEX adapter. Both results matched independently checked ledger data.
Recorded balance snapshot, not a current balance feed.

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
One stroop. Confirmed.
A real chat request sent 0.0000001 Testnet XLM. Orloj retained the hash and confirmed success before reporting completion.
Historical confirmed transfer. No transaction is sent by this showcase.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Recover the result. Never repeat the payment.
A provider interruption did not erase the operation. Read-only status recovery returned the original confirmed hash and an exact fee string.
Earlier provider and arithmetic failures were documented and corrected.

7
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Evidence over promises.
39 confirmed Testnet transactions, including funding and setup. 168 checks passed. Eleven ranked entries audited; five have Testnet write coverage.
Provider quotas, unsupported signatures and privileged roles still apply. No hosted backend or mainnet writes.
